-- תקנון שירות עובדי הוראה, פרק 1א', §1.12 תפקידים וגמולים
-- Role-holders and their allowances: the closed list of roles, who appoints
-- them and on what terms, the base and the scaling of the allowances, and
-- the rules of each allowance (class education, subject and
-- qualifications, coordinations, counselling, boarding supervision,
-- security, technical coordination, training).

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT common

§ `1.12 תפקידים וגמולים`

GIVEN d IS A DATE, e IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE d `is on or after` e IF
    DATE_SERIAL d AT LEAST DATE_SERIAL e

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p1 An amendment note: the section was updated on 29.1.03.

§§ `כללי`

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p2 A heading: "כללי".

-- ¶3, ¶5, ¶7: the agreement of 16.11.83 closed the list of roles and their
-- allowances; road-safety coordination was added to it. (The split-position
-- allowance is section 1.11.)
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p3 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p5 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p7
DECLARE `role allowance` IS ONE OF
    `class education`
    `subject and qualifications`
    `subject coordination`
    `grade-level, track, stream or class-group coordination`
    `social coordination`
    `laboratory coordination`
    `teacher-counsellor`
    `boarding-school supervision`
    `security officer`
    `technical coordination in vocational centres`
    `training`
    `guidance coordination`
    `road-safety coordination`

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p6 A pointer: the split-position allowance is section 1.11.

-- ¶4: criteria the agreement did not change stay as they were.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p4
GIVEN `the agreement changed the criterion` IS A BOOLEAN
      `criterion as changed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `criterion before the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the criterion in force` `the agreement changed the criterion` `criterion as changed` `criterion before the agreement` IF
    IF `the agreement changed the criterion`
    THEN `criterion as changed`
    ELSE `criterion before the agreement`

-- ¶8: the school further-training coordinator was abolished with that
-- training, so it is not on the list. ¶9 "תחולה 1.9.94" follows the
-- addition (¶7) and the abolition and names neither; F-1.12-h: the reading
-- adopted is the date of both.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p8 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p9
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the school further-training coordinator is a role on` d IF
    NOT (d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 1994))

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `road-safety coordination is on the list on` d IF
    d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 1994)

-- F-1.12-h's evidence: the changes ¶9's date line follows, which it does not name.
`the changes ¶9's date could govern` MEANS
    LIST "¶7: road-safety coordination added to the list",
         "¶8: the school further-training coordinator abolished"
`¶9's date follows two changes and names neither` MEANS
    count `the changes ¶9's date could govern` EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `¶9's date follows two changes and names neither`

§§ `1. המינוי`

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p10 A heading: "המינוי".

@desc A proposed appointment of a teaching employee to a role.
DECLARE `appointment` HAS
    `role`                                      IS A `role allowance`
    `made by the principal`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `approved by the general supervisor`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the subject supervisor was consulted`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `position fraction of the appointee`        IS A NUMBER
    `roles the appointee already holds`         IS A LIST OF `role allowance`
    `the district manager found an essential need` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the appointee is a principal`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `classes the principal would educate`       IS A NUMBER
    `the appointee is a vice-principal`         IS A BOOLEAN

@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p11
GIVEN a IS AN `appointment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `properly made` a IF
        a's `made by the principal`
    AND a's `approved by the general supervisor`
    AND a's `the subject supervisor was consulted`

-- ¶17: subject and qualifications is not a "role" for ¶13–16.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p17
GIVEN r IS A `role allowance`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a role for the appointment limits` r IF
    (NOT (r EQUALS `subject and qualifications`))

@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p13
GIVEN a IS AN `appointment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `holds a third of a position` a IF
    a's `position fraction of the appointee` AT LEAST 1/3

@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p14
GIVEN a IS AN `appointment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `within the limit of two roles` a IF
        count (filter `is a role for the appointment limits` (a's `roles the appointee already holds`)) LESS THAN 2
    OR  a's `the district manager found an essential need`

-- ¶15–16: a principal takes no further role but the education of one class;
-- a vice-principal may add class education or security. F-1.12-g: whether
-- ¶16 only permits those two or also limits the vice-principal to them is
-- not said; the reading adopted is ¶15's counterpart, a limit.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p15 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p16
GIVEN a IS AN `appointment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `allowed for a principal` a IF
        (NOT a's `the appointee is a principal`)
    OR  (NOT `is a role for the appointment limits` (a's `role`))
    OR  (a's `role` EQUALS `class education` AND a's `classes the principal would educate` AT MOST 1)

GIVEN a IS AN `appointment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `allowed for a vice-principal` a IF
        (NOT a's `the appointee is a vice-principal`)
    OR  (NOT `is a role for the appointment limits` (a's `role`))
    OR  a's `role` EQUALS `class education`
    OR  a's `role` EQUALS `security officer`

-- F-1.12-g's evidence: a vice-principal asked to coordinate a laboratory
-- passes every other rule of appointment, and only ¶16 read as a limit bars him.
`a vice-principal asked to coordinate a laboratory` MEANS
    `appointment` WITH
        `role`                                      IS `laboratory coordination`
        `made by the principal`                     IS TRUE
        `approved by the general supervisor`        IS TRUE
        `the subject supervisor was consulted`      IS TRUE
        `position fraction of the appointee`        IS 1
        `roles the appointee already holds`         IS EMPTY
        `the district manager found an essential need` IS FALSE
        `the appointee is a principal`              IS FALSE
        `classes the principal would educate`       IS 0
        `the appointee is a vice-principal`         IS TRUE

`only ¶16 read as a limit bars a vice-principal from coordinating a laboratory` MEANS
        `properly made` `a vice-principal asked to coordinate a laboratory`
    AND `holds a third of a position` `a vice-principal asked to coordinate a laboratory`
    AND `within the limit of two roles` `a vice-principal asked to coordinate a laboratory`
    AND `allowed for a principal` `a vice-principal asked to coordinate a laboratory`
    AND (NOT `allowed for a vice-principal` `a vice-principal asked to coordinate a laboratory`)
#ASSERT `only ¶16 read as a limit bars a vice-principal from coordinating a laboratory`

-- ¶18: the same rules govern the road-safety coordinator.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p18
GIVEN a IS AN `appointment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may be appointed` a IF
        `properly made` a
    AND (    (NOT `is a role for the appointment limits` (a's `role`))
         OR  (    `holds a third of a position` a
              AND `within the limit of two roles` a
              AND `allowed for a principal` a
              AND `allowed for a vice-principal` a))

-- ¶12: for one school year, and no hold on the role.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p12
`months an appointment lasts` MEANS 12

GIVEN `months since the appointment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appointment still runs` `months since the appointment` IF
    `months since the appointment` LESS THAN `months an appointment lasts`

§§ `2. הגמולים`

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p19 A heading: "הגמולים".

@desc A teaching employee holding a role, as section 1.12.2 asks about her.
DECLARE `role-holder` HAS
    `allowance held`                    IS A `role allowance`
    `fills the role now`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `actual position fraction`          IS A NUMBER
    `full-position base`                IS A NUMBER @desc the combined salary for one full position by grade and seniority, with the 3% (2001), 5% (2008), 4% (2011) and 1994 teaching supplements (section 1.12.2א); an input until section 1.1 is imported
    `allowance rate`                    IS A NUMBER @desc the allowance's rate, from its own paragraph below

-- ¶20: the base; ¶23: paid on one full position whatever the actual
-- position, except subject and qualifications and the teacher-counsellor.
-- The counsellor's own rule (¶67–72) scales the RATE by counselling hours
-- and puts it on one full position, so its factor here is 1.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p20 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p23
DECLARE `base component` IS ONE OF
    `the combined salary by grade and teaching seniority`
    `the 3% supplement (2001 agreement)`
    `the 5% supplement (2008 agreement)`
    `the 4% supplement (2011 agreement)`
    `the 1994 teaching supplement`

`the components of the allowances' base` MEANS
    LIST `the combined salary by grade and teaching seniority`, `the 3% supplement (2001 agreement)`,
         `the 5% supplement (2008 agreement)`, `the 4% supplement (2011 agreement)`, `the 1994 teaching supplement`

GIVEN r IS A `role allowance`, fraction IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `position factor for` r fraction IS
    IF r EQUALS `subject and qualifications`
    THEN fraction
    ELSE 1

-- ¶21: paid while the role is filled, stopped when it is not.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p21
@export default The role allowance (gemul tafkid) a teaching employee is owed for a month under section 1.12 of the takanon, from its rate
GIVEN h IS A `role-holder` @desc the employee and the allowance
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `role allowance amount` h IS
    IF h's `fills the role now`
    THEN h's `allowance rate` TIMES h's `full-position base`
             TIMES `position factor for` (h's `allowance held`) (h's `actual position fraction`)
    ELSE 0

-- ¶22: none of the allowances is salary for any purpose, but class
-- education and subject and qualifications; one that was salary for a
-- purpose before stays salary for it alone. ¶75 (counsellor) below.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p22
GIVEN r IS A `role allowance`, `was salary for this purpose before` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is salary under ¶22` r `was salary for this purpose before` IF
        r EQUALS `class education`
    OR  r EQUALS `subject and qualifications`
    OR  `was salary for this purpose before`

-- ¶24–30: allowances still paid in shekels, updated with the cost-of-living
-- supplements; the amounts are inputs.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p24 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p25 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p28 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p30
DECLARE `shekel allowance` IS ONE OF
    `security officer, up to 15 classes, not on the teaching scale`
    `security officer, 15 classes or more, not on the teaching scale`
    `assistant security officer in a boarding school, not on the teaching scale`
    `assistant security officer in a boarding school outside a local authority`
    `guiding a pupil's final project in a post-primary school`

-- The two rows of ¶26–27 AS PRINTED, by the institution's number of
-- classes. F-1.12-a: both take an institution of exactly 15 classes.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p26 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p27
GIVEN classes IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF `shekel allowance`
DECIDE `the security rows that take` classes IS
    filter (GIVEN s YIELD
                CONSIDER s
                WHEN `security officer, up to 15 classes, not on the teaching scale` THEN classes AT MOST 15
                WHEN `security officer, 15 classes or more, not on the teaching scale` THEN classes AT LEAST 15
                OTHERWISE FALSE)
           (LIST `security officer, up to 15 classes, not on the teaching scale`,
                 `security officer, 15 classes or more, not on the teaching scale`)

`an institution of 15 classes falls in both security rows` MEANS
    count (`the security rows that take` 15) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `an institution of 15 classes falls in both security rows`

-- The reading adopted (F-1.12-a): the row that OPENS at 15 governs it.
GIVEN classes IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `shekel allowance`
DECIDE `the security shekel row for` classes IS
    IF classes AT LEAST 15
    THEN `security officer, 15 classes or more, not on the teaching scale`
    ELSE `security officer, up to 15 classes, not on the teaching scale`

-- F-1.12-d: ¶29 (assistant in a boarding school outside a local authority,
-- in SHEKELS, with no "not on the teaching scale" as rows 1–3 have) and ¶98
-- (the same assistant at 5%, a percentage "from 1.11.1983") both take an
-- assistant on the teaching scale. The reading adopted gives row 4 the same
-- limit as rows 1–3: it is for those not on the teaching scale.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p29
GIVEN `on the teaching scale` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `paid row 4 in shekels` `on the teaching scale` IF
    (NOT `on the teaching scale`)

-- The five rows of ¶26–30 as printed: does the row say "not on the teaching scale"?
GIVEN s IS A `shekel allowance`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the printed row is limited to those off the teaching scale` s IF
    CONSIDER s
    WHEN `assistant security officer in a boarding school outside a local authority` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `guiding a pupil's final project in a post-primary school` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

`row 4 as printed and ¶98 both take a teaching-scale assistant outside a local authority` MEANS
        (NOT `the printed row is limited to those off the teaching scale` `assistant security officer in a boarding school outside a local authority`)
    AND `percentage for a security role` `assistant in a boarding school outside a local authority` GREATER THAN 0
#ASSERT `row 4 as printed and ¶98 both take a teaching-scale assistant outside a local authority`

§§ `3. חינוך כיתה`

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p31 A heading: "חינוך כיתה".

DECLARE `educator` IS ONE OF
    `the educator of a class, so determined by the principal`
    `a kindergarten teacher`
    `a kindergarten teacher with the kindergarten-coordination allowance`
    `a teacher of assisted-teaching classes`
    `an assistant kindergarten teacher`
    `an inclusion kindergarten teacher`
    `a rabbi-teacher (ר"מ)`
    `a school rabbi`
    `an educator of grades 13–14`
    `a pedagogic instructor in a teacher-training college`
    `the teacher in charge of an adult-education class`
    `someone else`

@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p32 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p33
GIVEN e IS AN `educator`, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `entitled to class education` e d IF
    CONSIDER e
    WHEN `the educator of a class, so determined by the principal` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a kindergarten teacher with the kindergarten-coordination allowance` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `someone else` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 11 1983)

-- ¶34: 10% from 1.1.01; ¶36: twice for two classes.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p34 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p36
GIVEN `classes educated` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `class-education rate` `classes educated` IS
    10% TIMES min `classes educated` 2

-- ¶35 and ¶42: both are salary for every purpose from 1.11.83.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p35 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p42
GIVEN r IS A `role allowance`, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is salary for every purpose` r d IF
        (r EQUALS `class education` OR r EQUALS `subject and qualifications`)
    AND (d `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 11 1983))

-- ¶37 and ¶43 (the same words twice): not both.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p37 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p43
GIVEN held IS A LIST OF `role allowance`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `class education and subject and qualifications are not held together` held IF
    (NOT (elem `class education` held AND elem `subject and qualifications` held))

§§ `4. מקצוע והכשרות`

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p38 A heading: "מקצוע והכשרות".

DECLARE `other allowance held` IS ONE OF
    `kindergarten coordination`, `class education held`, `management`,
    `teacher-instructor`, `guidance`, `supervision`, `none of these`

-- ¶39: every teaching employee, but those holding one of six allowances;
-- teachers in guidance roles in some cases (section 8.1.6.1, an input).
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p39
GIVEN o IS AN `other allowance held`
      `entitled by section 8.1.6.1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc a teacher in a guidance role whom section 8.1.6.1 entitles to this allowance; an input until that section is imported
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `entitled to subject and qualifications` o `entitled by section 8.1.6.1` IF
    o EQUALS `none of these` OR `entitled by section 8.1.6.1`

-- ¶40–41: 6% from 1.1.01, on the actual position, below or above one.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p40 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p41
`subject and qualifications rate` MEANS 6%

§§ `5. ריכוז מקצוע`

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p44 A heading: "ריכוז מקצוע".

@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p45
DECLARE `subject coordinator` IS ONE OF
    `a subject coordinator`
    `a domain coordinator (a cluster of subjects, e.g. arts education or KKL heritage)`
    `a coordinator agreed between the Ministry and the teachers' organisations`

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p46 A pointer: appointment and allowance in a primary school are in section 3.14.
-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p47 A pointer: appointment and allowance in a post-primary school are in section 6.10.

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p48 A heading: "ריכוז בטיחות בדרכים".

DECLARE `appointment duty` IS ONE OF
    `appoint a road-safety coordinator`
    `appoint a security officer`
    `appoint an assistant security officer`
    `set the division of security tasks`
    `allot weekly hours to the security officer` HAS `weekly hours allotted` IS A NUMBER

-- ¶49: every school appoints one, at 6%; ¶50: on passing the road-safety
-- course and with the road-safety supervisor's approval.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p49
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `appointment duty`
DECIDE `every school appoints a road-safety coordinator` IS
    PARTY `the school principal`
    MUST  `appoint a road-safety coordinator`
    LEST BREACH BY `the school principal` BECAUSE "section 1.12: in every school a road-safety coordinator is appointed"

`road-safety coordination rate` MEANS 6%

@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p50
GIVEN `passed the road-safety course` IS A BOOLEAN, `approved by the road-safety supervisor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may fill road-safety coordination` `passed the road-safety course` `approved by the road-safety supervisor` IF
    `passed the road-safety course` AND `approved by the road-safety supervisor`

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p51 A heading: "ריכוז שכבה/מסלול/מגמה/חטיבת כיתות".

DECLARE `kind of school` IS ONE OF `primary`, `post-primary`, `other school`

-- ¶52 and ¶55: one coordinator per school, primary and post-primary only.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p52 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p55
GIVEN k IS A `kind of school`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `coordinators paid per school` k IS
    IF k EQUALS `other school` THEN 0 ELSE 1

@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p53
`grade-level coordination rate` MEANS 6%

§§ `6. ריכוז חברתי`

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p54 A heading: "ריכוז חברתי".

@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p56
`social coordination rate` MEANS 6%

-- ¶57: in a post-primary school one coordinator takes it all; two or three
-- share it; beyond that the others take none. F-1.12-c: the share is not
-- stated; the reading adopted divides the one allowance equally.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p57
GIVEN k IS A `kind of school`, coordinators IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `social coordination rate of each` k coordinators IS
    BRANCH IF coordinators LESS THAN 1 THEN 0
           IF (NOT (k EQUALS `post-primary`)) THEN `social coordination rate`
           IF coordinators AT MOST 3 THEN `social coordination rate` DIVIDED BY coordinators
           OTHERWISE `social coordination rate` DIVIDED BY 3

-- What ¶57 states as the share of each of two or three coordinators, as
-- printed: nothing.
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the share ¶57 states for each of two or three coordinators` IS
    NOTHING
`¶57 states no share for two or three social coordinators` MEANS
    isNothing `the share ¶57 states for each of two or three coordinators`
#ASSERT `¶57 states no share for two or three social coordinators`

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p58 A heading: "ריכוז מעבדה/מרכזייה פדגוגית מוסדית/אמצעי הוראה".

-- ¶59: one coordinator only (laboratory, pedagogic centre or teaching aids)
-- in an institution with any of grades 1–14. ¶62–63: the RATES of ¶60–61
-- are for institutions outside post-primary education; post-primary ones
-- appoint by the existing criteria (section 6.9.2) and at least one.
-- F-1.12-e: for a post-primary institution ¶59 says one only and ¶63 lets
-- section 6.9.2 give more; the reading adopted is ¶63 for post-primary.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p59 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p62 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p63
GIVEN k IS A `kind of school`, `coordinators the criteria of 6.9.2 allow` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `laboratory coordinators allowed` k `coordinators the criteria of 6.9.2 allow` IS
    IF k EQUALS `post-primary`
    THEN max 1 `coordinators the criteria of 6.9.2 allow`
    ELSE 1

`¶59 and ¶63 part where section 6.9.2 allows two` MEANS
    (NOT (`laboratory coordinators allowed` `post-primary` 2 EQUALS 1))
#ASSERT `¶59 and ¶63 part where section 6.9.2 allows two`

@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p60 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p61
GIVEN classes IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `laboratory coordination rate` classes IS
    IF classes AT LEAST 13 THEN 5% ELSE 3%

§§ `7. מורה-יועץ`

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p64 A heading: "מורה-יועץ".

@desc A teacher-counsellor, as section 1.12.7 asks about her.
DECLARE `counsellor` HAS
    `holds a counselling licence`               IS A BOOLEAN @desc section 3.12.2
    `weekly counselling hours`                  IS A NUMBER
    `full rate for the years of counselling`    IS A NUMBER @desc the full counselling rate for her years of counselling seniority; ¶66 says a table gives it, and none follows (F-1.12-b) — an input

@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p65
GIVEN c IS A `counsellor`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `entitled to the counselling allowance` c IF
    c's `holds a counselling licence`

-- F-1.12-b: "הגמול יחושב כמפורט בטבלה להלן" — no table follows, in the
-- corpus or in the ministry's published page; the full rate by years of
-- counselling is therefore an input.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p66
`the rows of the counselling table the text prints` MEANS
    EMPTY

`¶66 refers to a table that is not there` MEANS
    null `the rows of the counselling table the text prints`
#ASSERT `¶66 refers to a table that is not there`

-- ¶67–71: 12 weekly hours earn the full rate; under 4 nothing; between them
-- the full rate times hours over 12; above 12 no more. "Allowance" there is
-- the number of percentage points.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p67 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p68 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p69 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p70 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p71
GIVEN c IS A `counsellor`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `counselling rate` c IS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `entitled to the counselling allowance` c) THEN 0
           IF c's `weekly counselling hours` LESS THAN 4 THEN 0
           IF c's `weekly counselling hours` AT LEAST 12 THEN c's `full rate for the years of counselling`
           OTHERWISE (c's `full rate for the years of counselling` TIMES c's `weekly counselling hours`) DIVIDED BY 12

-- ¶72: on the salary of one full position.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p72
GIVEN c IS A `counsellor`, `full-position salary` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `counselling allowance` c `full-position salary` IS
    `counselling rate` c TIMES `full-position salary`

@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p73
GIVEN `receives the counselling allowance` IS A BOOLEAN, `training was for the counselling certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `further-training allowance for that training` `receives the counselling allowance` `training was for the counselling certificate` IF
    (NOT (`receives the counselling allowance` AND `training was for the counselling certificate`))

-- ¶74: no tenure in the role; counselling hours may be turned into teaching
-- hours; tenure is on the position only.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p74
GIVEN `position before` IS A NUMBER, `counselling hours turned into teaching` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `position kept when counselling ends` `position before` `counselling hours turned into teaching` IS
    `position before`

-- ¶75: counselling of at least half a position (6 hours) for at least 5
-- years before retirement, not counted before, is pensionable. F-1.12-f:
-- ¶22 says no allowance but two is salary for any purpose unless it was
-- before; ¶75 makes this one pensionable exactly where it was not. The
-- reading adopted: ¶75, the particular clause, governs the counsellor.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p75
GIVEN `weekly counselling hours in the last years` IS A NUMBER
      `years of such counselling before retirement` IS A NUMBER
      `counted for pension before` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the counselling allowance is pensionable`
        `weekly counselling hours in the last years`
        `years of such counselling before retirement`
        `counted for pension before` IF
        `counted for pension before`
    OR  (    `weekly counselling hours in the last years` AT LEAST 6
         AND `years of such counselling before retirement` AT LEAST 5)

`¶22 and ¶75 part on a counsellor's pension` MEANS
        `the counselling allowance is pensionable` 6 5 FALSE
    AND (NOT `is salary under ¶22` `teacher-counsellor` FALSE)
#ASSERT `¶22 and ¶75 part on a counsellor's pension`

-- ¶76–78: eight years of counselling, one of them in the last seven before
-- the move, carry the allowance into teaching (from 1.1.93); not into
-- management, supervision or a college; back in teaching after those, the
-- allowance of the eve of that appointment returns.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p76 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p77 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p78
DECLARE `move after counselling` IS ONE OF
    `to teaching`
    `to principal or vice-principal`
    `to guidance and supervision`
    `to teaching in a seminar or college`

GIVEN `years of counselling` IS A NUMBER
      `a counselling year among the last seven` IS A BOOLEAN
      move IS A `move after counselling`
      `date of the move` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `carries the counselling allowance`
        `years of counselling` `a counselling year among the last seven` move `date of the move` IF
        `years of counselling` AT LEAST 8
    AND `a counselling year among the last seven`
    AND move EQUALS `to teaching`
    AND (`date of the move` `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 1993))

-- ¶78: back in teaching after one of those roles, the counselling allowance
-- of the eve of that appointment.
GIVEN `counselling allowance on the eve of that appointment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `counselling allowance on returning to teaching` `counselling allowance on the eve of that appointment` IS
    `counselling allowance on the eve of that appointment`

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p79 A heading: "השגחה על פנימייה".

§§ `השגחה על פנימייה`

@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p80 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p81 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p82
GIVEN `post-primary with a boarding school or afternoon studies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `receives other pay for the afternoon or the boarding school` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another employee is paid for this role` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `boarding-supervision rate`
        `post-primary with a boarding school or afternoon studies`
        `receives other pay for the afternoon or the boarding school`
        `another employee is paid for this role` IS
    IF      `post-primary with a boarding school or afternoon studies`
        AND (NOT `receives other pay for the afternoon or the boarding school`)
        AND (NOT `another employee is paid for this role`)
    THEN 5%
    ELSE 0

§§ `אחראי על ביטחון`

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p83 A heading: "אחראי על ביטחון".
-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p84 A heading: "מינוי האחראי לביטחון".

-- ¶85, ¶87: the principal appoints one every year before the school year
-- opens (time in months from 1 August; the year opens at 1); if none is
-- appointed, the principal fills the role.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p85 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p87
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `appointment duty`
DECIDE `the principal appoints a security officer` IS
    PARTY `the school principal`
    MUST  `appoint a security officer`
    WITHIN 1
    LEST BREACH BY `the school principal` BECAUSE "section 1.12: a security officer is appointed each year before the school year opens"

GIVEN `a security officer was appointed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the principal fills the security officer's role` `a security officer was appointed` IF
    NOT `a security officer was appointed`

-- ¶86: a vice-principal or member of the management, with organising
-- ability, at the institution most days; military training is desirable,
-- not required.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p86
GIVEN `is a vice-principal or management member` IS A BOOLEAN
      `has organising ability` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at the institution most days of the week` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may be the security officer`
        `is a vice-principal or management member` `has organising ability` `at the institution most days of the week` IF
    `is a vice-principal or management member` AND `has organising ability` AND `at the institution most days of the week`

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p88 A heading: "תנאי שירות".

-- ¶89: the role carries an allowance only; with spare hours in the
-- management quota, the principal may allot it up to 2 weekly hours.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p89
GIVEN `spare hours in the management quota` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `appointment duty`
DECIDE `hours for the security officer` `spare hours in the management quota` IS
    IF `spare hours in the management quota`
    THEN PARTY `the school principal`
         MAY   `allot weekly hours to the security officer` n
               PROVIDED n AT MOST 2
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- ¶90: a boarding institution has an assistant too, also paid, and the
-- officer divides the work with him; ¶91: a principal who fills the role is
-- not paid; ¶94–98: the rates, for one duly appointed.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p90 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p91 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p94 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p95 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p96 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p97 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p98
DECLARE `security role` IS ONE OF
    `security officer`
    `assistant in a boarding school`
    `assistant in a boarding school outside a local authority`
    `a principal filling the role himself`

GIVEN r IS A `security role`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `percentage for a security role` r IS
    CONSIDER r
    WHEN `security officer` THEN 6%
    WHEN `assistant in a boarding school` THEN 4%
    WHEN `assistant in a boarding school outside a local authority` THEN 5%
    WHEN `a principal filling the role himself` THEN 0

GIVEN `the institution has a boarding school` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `appointment duty`
DECIDE `an assistant security officer is appointed` `the institution has a boarding school` IS
    IF `the institution has a boarding school`
    THEN PARTY `the school principal`
         MUST  `appoint an assistant security officer`
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- ¶92: the principal bears overall responsibility, and a division of the
-- daily tasks between him and the officer must be set.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p92
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `appointment duty`
DECIDE `a division of security tasks is set` IS
    PARTY `the school principal`
    MUST  `set the division of security tasks`
    LEST BREACH BY `the school principal` BECAUSE "section 1.12: the daily security tasks are divided between the principal and the officer"

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p93 A heading: "הגמול".

§§ `ריכוז טכני במפת"נים`

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p99 A heading: "ריכוז טכני במפת\"נים".

DECLARE `vocational trade` IS ONE OF `wood`, `metal`, `shoemaking`, `vehicles`, `another trade`

@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p100 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p101
GIVEN t IS A `vocational trade`, `another technical coordinator is paid there` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `technical coordination rate` t `another technical coordinator is paid there` IS
    IF (NOT (t EQUALS `another trade`)) AND (NOT `another technical coordinator is paid there`)
    THEN 1%
    ELSE 0

§§ `אימון`

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p102 A heading: "אימון".

DECLARE `trainee` IS ONE OF
    `a pupil of a carer-educator track`
    `a first- or second-year college student`
    `a third-year college student`

@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p103 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p104 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p105 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p106 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p107
GIVEN t IS A `trainee`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `rate per trainee` t IS
    CONSIDER t
    WHEN `a third-year college student` THEN 2%
    OTHERWISE 1%

GIVEN trainees IS A LIST OF `trainee`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `training rate` trainees IS
    sum (map `rate per trainee` trainees)

-- ¶108: no more than 3 trainees to one trainer.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p108
GIVEN trainees IS A LIST OF `trainee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `within the limit of trainees` trainees IF
    count trainees AT MOST 3

-- ¶109: a shorter training period, negotiated with the college, is paid for
-- the months trained, with their part of the summer break.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p109
GIVEN `months trained` IS A NUMBER, `months of a full training year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `share of the training allowance` `months trained` `months of a full training year` IS
    min 1 (`months trained` DIVIDED BY `months of a full training year`)

@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p110
GIVEN `trains on a regular basis` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `extra pay for concentrated training` `trains on a regular basis` IS
    0

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p111 A pointer: seminar guidance coordination is in section 11.6.3.

-- Worked examples. Every salary figure is a placeholder.
`a class educator of two classes` MEANS
    `role-holder` WITH
        `allowance held`            IS `class education`
        `fills the role now`        IS TRUE
        `actual position fraction`  IS 0.5
        `full-position base`        IS 10000
        `allowance rate`            IS `class-education rate` 2

#ASSERT `role allowance amount` `a class educator of two classes` EQUALS 2000

`a counsellor of 6 hours` MEANS
    `counsellor` WITH
        `holds a counselling licence`            IS TRUE
        `weekly counselling hours`               IS 6
        `full rate for the years of counselling` IS 10%

#ASSERT `counselling rate` `a counsellor of 6 hours` EQUALS 5%
-- (This example used to give four trainees 5%, paying for the first three:
-- a cut-off the text does not state. ¶108 is a limit, asked directly.)
#ASSERT `training rate` (LIST `a third-year college student`, `a third-year college student`, `a first- or second-year college student`) EQUALS 5%
#ASSERT (NOT `within the limit of trainees` (LIST `a third-year college student`, `a third-year college student`, `a first- or second-year college student`, `a third-year college student`))
#ASSERT `laboratory coordination rate` 12 EQUALS 3%

`a principal asked to coordinate a subject` MEANS
    `appointment` WITH
        `role`                                      IS `subject coordination`
        `made by the principal`                     IS TRUE
        `approved by the general supervisor`        IS TRUE
        `the subject supervisor was consulted`      IS TRUE
        `position fraction of the appointee`        IS 1
        `roles the appointee already holds`         IS EMPTY
        `the district manager found an essential need` IS FALSE
        `the appointee is a principal`              IS TRUE
        `classes the principal would educate`       IS 0
        `the appointee is a vice-principal`         IS FALSE
#ASSERT (NOT `may be appointed` `a principal asked to coordinate a subject`)

#TRACE `hours for the security officer` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the school principal` DOES `allot weekly hours to the security officer` 2 AT 1
#TRACE `the principal appoints a security officer` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the school principal` DOES `appoint a security officer` AT 1

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p112 The heading of the section's sources (אסמכתא).
-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p113 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p114 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p115 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p116 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p117 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p118 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p119 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p120 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p121 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p122 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p123 The sources themselves (1–11).
-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p124 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p125 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p126 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p127 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p128 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p129 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p130 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p131 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p132 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_12__ssec_1_12/p133 The sources themselves (12–21).
